# A reverse two-core certificate for the first involution census pair

The explicit dihedral conjugator for census representative 2 carries the
marked involution into kernel word 5722. These checked packed products are
the arithmetic input to the literal conjugation identities in `FirstPair`.
They use the original ATLAS J4G1-f2r112B0, J4G1-max2W1 words and increasing
kernel-bit convention; see LocalInvolutionCensus/Fusion/source/README.md.

Source motivation: Kleidman--Wilson, The Maximal Subgroups of J4 (1988),
p.487, Lemma 1.1.3 and Corollary 1.1.4. This is one actual pair calculation,
not a proof of the full four-group table or its symmetry assertion.
-/

